`MAX_EXPR_NESTING` is 3, which limits the nesting of expressions inside f-strings. So we can't nest f-strings more than 3 levels deep through expressions. The tokenizer will raise a "f-string: expressions nested too deeply" error before we can get to 200 levels.

So the off-by-one error must be triggered differently. Let me re-read the fix commit more carefully. The fix added a check at line 2235 (in the fixed version) before `TOK_NEXT_MODE`:

```c
if (tok->tok_mode_stack_index + 1 >= MAXFSTRINGLEVEL) {
    return MAKE_TOKEN(syntaxerror(tok, "too many nested f-strings"));
}
```

